    "description": "# napari-freeimagetovideo\n\nFree image to video AI with no daily cap: start with no sign-up, keep going on a free account. Every video comes with sound and no watermark.\n\nA [napari](https://napari.org/) plugin for [Free Image to Video (freeimagetovideo.ai)](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/?utm_source=napari&utm_medium=package) that generates AI video clips from a text prompt or public image URL using MiniMax H3 and loads the decoded MP4 frames directly as a time-series RGB image layer.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install napari-freeimagetovideo\n```\n\nCreate an API key at [freeimagetovideo.ai/settings/apikeys](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/settings/apikeys) and set `FREEIMAGETOVIDEO_API_KEY` (or enter it directly in the widget). API runs require a paid plan ([pricing](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/pricing)); browser generation starts with no sign-up at [freeimagetovideo.ai](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/).\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open napari and choose **Plugins -> Free Image to Video AI**.\n2. Enter a motion prompt, optional public image URL (first frame), duration (`4`\u2013`15` seconds), resolution (`480p` or `768p`), and aspect ratio (`16:9`, `9:16`, or `1:1`).\n3. Click **Generate** to append the rendered video frames as an RGB image stack layer.\n\n## Links\n\n- [Free Image to Video](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/?utm_source=napari&utm_medium=package)\n- [Free AI Video Generator (No Sign-Up)](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/video/free-ai-video-generator-no-sign-up)\n- [Animate Photo AI](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/video/animate-photo-ai)\n- [Pricing & Plans](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/pricing)\n- [API Keys](https://freeimagetovideo.ai/settings/apikeys)\n- [Documentation](https://freeimagetovideo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)\n\nMIT licensed.\n",
